{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Muslim ibn Aqeel (a.s.)",
  "data": "After the acts of Masjid al-Kufah, go to the tomb of Muslim ibn Aqil (a.s.). Standing at the tomb, say:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الْمَلِكِ الْحَقِّ الْمُبِيْنِ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL MALIKIL HAQQIL MUBEEN\nAll praise be to Allah: the Lord and the evident Truth.\nالْمُتَصَاغِرِ لِعَظَمَتِهٖ جَبَابِرَةُ الطَّاغِيْنَ\nAL-MUTASAAGHIRI LI-A'ZAMATIHEE JABAABIRATUT TAAGHEEN\nAll the tyrannical oppressors are subservient to His almightiness.\nالْمُعْتَرِفِ بِرُبُوْبِيَّتِهٖ جَمِيْعُ اَهْلِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرَضِيْنَ\nAL-MU'TARIFI BIRUBOOBIYYATIHEE JAMEE'U AHLIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARADEEN\nAll the inhabitants of the heavens and the layers of the earth admit His Godhead.\nالْمُقِرِّ بِتَوْحِيْدِهٖ سَاۤئِرُ الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nAL-MUQIRRI BITAWHEEDIHEE SAA'IRUL KHALQI AJMA'EEN\nAll the created beings confess of His Oneness.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِ الْاَنَامِ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA SAYYIDIL ANAAM\nMay Allah send blessings upon the master of all created beings\nوَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الْكِرَامِ\nWA AHLI BAYTIHIL KIRAAM\nand upon the members of his noble Household,\nصَلَاةً تَقَرُّ بِهَا اَعْيُنُهُمْ\nSALAATAN TAQARRU BIHAA A'YUNUHUM\nsuch blessings that delight them\nوَيَرْغَمُ بِهَا اَنْفُ شَانِئِهِمْ\nWA YARGHAMU BIHAA ANFU SHAANI'IHIM\nand humiliate all those who antagonize them\nمِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nMINAL JINNI WAL INSI AJMA'EEN\nfrom all jinn and mankind.\nسَلَامُ اللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSALAAMULLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nPeace of Allah the All-high and All-great,\nوَسَلَامُ مَلَاۤئِكَتِهِ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nWA SALAAMU MALAA'IKATIHIL MUQARRABEEN\nand peace of His favorite angels,\nوَاَنْبِيَاۤئِهِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nWA ANBIYAA'IHIL MURSALEEN\nHis missioned Prophets,\nوَاَئِمَّتِهِ الْمُنْتَجَبِيْنَ\nWA A'IMMATIHIL MUNTAJABEEN\nHis choice Imams,\nوَعِبَادِهِ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA I'BAADIHIS SAALIHEEN\nHis righteous servants,\nوَجَمِيْعِ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ وَالصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ\nWA JAMEE'ISH SHUHADAA'I WAS SIDDEEQEEN\nand all the martyrs and veracious ones,\nوَالزَّاكِيَاتُ الطَّيِّبَاتُ\nWAZ ZAAKIYAATUT TAYYIBAAT\nand all pure and goodly blessings\nفِيْمَا تَغْتَدِيْ وَتَرُوْحُ\nFEEMAA TAGHTADEE WA TAROOH\nthat are coming and going,\nعَلَيْكَ يَا مُسْلِمَ بْنَ عَقِيْلِ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nA'LAYKA YAA MUSLIMABNA A'QEELIBNI ABEE TAALIB\nbe upon you, O Muslim son of Aqil son of Abu Talib,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand Allah’s mercy and blessings.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA AQAMTAS SALAAH\nI bear witness that you performed the prayers,\nوَاٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ\nWA AATAYTAZ ZAKAAH\ndefrayed the zakat,\nوَاَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ\nWA AMARTA BIL MA'ROOF\nenjoined the right,\nوَنَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nWA NAHAYTA A'NIL MUNKAR\nforbade the wrong,\nوَجَاهَدْتَ فِي اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ\nWA JAAHADTA FILLAAHI HAQQA JIHAADIH\nstrove in the way of Allah in the best manner of striving,\nوَقُتِلْتَ عَلٰى مِنْهَاجِ الْمُجَاهِدِيْنَ فِيْ سَبِيْلِهٖ\nWA QUTILTA A'LAA MINHAAJIL MUJAAHIDEENA FEE SABEELIH\nand you were slain following the course of those who strive in Allah’s way\nحَتّٰى لَقِيْتَ اللّٰهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ وَهُوَ عَنْكَ رَاضٍ\nHATTAA LAQEETALLAAHA A'ZZA WA JALLA WA HUWA A'NKA RAAD\nuntil you met Allah, to Whom belong all might and majesty, while He is pleased with you.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ وَفَيْتَ بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA WAFAYTA BI-A'HDILLAAH\nAnd I bear witness that you fulfilled your covenant with Allah\nوَبَذَلْتَ نَفْسَكَ فِي نُصْرَةِ حُجَّةِ اللّٰهِ وَابْنِ حُجَّتِهٖ\nWA BADHALTA NAFSAKA FEE NUSRATI HUJJATILLAAHI WABNI HUJJATIH\nand sacrificed yourself for the sake of supporting Allah’s argument and the son of Allah’s argument (namely, Imam al-Husayn)\nحَتّٰى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nHATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nuntil death came upon you.\nاَشْهَدُ لَكَ بِالتَّسْلِيْمِ وَالْوَفَاۤءِ\nASH-HADU LAKA BIT TASLEEMI WAL WAFAA'\nI bear witness that you submitted and acted loyally to him\nوَالنَّصِيْحَةِ لِخَلَفِ النَّبِيِّ الْمُرْسَلِ\nWAN NASEEHATI LIKHALAFIN NABIYYIL MURSAL\nand that you acted sincerely to the successor of the missioned Prophet,\nوَالسِّبْطِ الْمُنْتَجَبِ\nWAS SIBTIL MUNTAJAB\nthe select grandson (of the Prophet),\nوَالدَّلِيْلِ الْعَالِمِ\nWAD DALEELIL A'ALIM\nthe guide (to the right path), the knowledgeable,\nوَالْوَصِيِّ الْمُبَلِّغِ\nWAL WASIYYIL MUBALLIGH\nthe Prophet’s successor, the conveyor (of his mission),\nوَالْمَظْلُوْمِ الْمُهْتَضَمِ\nWAL MAZLOOMIL MUHTADAM\nthe wronged, and the oppressed Imam.\nفَجَزَاكَ اللّٰهُ عَنْ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nFAJAZAAKALLAAHU A'N RASOOLIH\nMay Allah reward you on behalf of His Messenger,\nوَعَنْ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nWA A'N AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\non behalf of the Commander of the Faithful,\nوَعَنِ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ\nWA A'NIL HASANI WAL HUSAYN\nand on behalf of al-Hasan and al-Husayn\nاَفْضَلَ الْجَزَاۤءِ\nAFDALAL JAZAA'\nwith the best of rewarding\nبِمَا صَبَرْتَ وَاحْتَسَبْتَ وَاَعَنْتَ\nBIMAA SABARTA WAHTASABTA WA A'ANT\nthat befits your steadfastness, reliance (on Allah), and assistance.\nفَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ\nFANI'MA U'QBAD DAAR\nHow excellent is the final home!\nلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ\nLA'ANALLAAHU MAN QATALAK\nMay Allah curse him who slew you.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ اَمَرَ بِقَتْلِكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN AMARA BIQATLIK\nMay Allah curse him who ordered of slaying you.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ ظَلَمَكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN ZALAMAK\nMay Allah curse him who wronged you.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَيْكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MANIF TARAA A'LAYK\nMay Allah curse him who forged lies against you.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ جَهِلَ حَقَّكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN JAHILA HAQQAK\nMay Allah curse him who underestimated your position\nوَاسْتَخَفَّ بِحُرْمَتِكَ\nWASTAKHAFFA BIHURMATIK\nand belittled your sanctity.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ بَايَعَكَ وَغَشَّكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN BAAYA'AKA WA GHASHSHAK\nMay Allah curse those who cheated you after they had sworn allegiance to you,\nوَخَذَلَكَ وَاَسْلَمَكَ\nWA KHADHALAKA WA ASLAMAK\nthose who disappointed and let you down,\nوَمَنْ اَلَّبَ عَلَيْكَ وَلَمْ يُعِنْكَ\nWA MAN ALLABA A'LAYKA WA LAM YU'INK\nand those who allied against you instead of assisting you.\nالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ جَعَلَ النَّارَ مَثْوَاهُمْ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALAN NAARA MATHWAAHUM\nAll praise be to Allah Who decided Hellfire to be the eternal abode of those peoples.\nوَبِئْسَ الْوِرْدُ الْمَوْرُوْدُ\nWA BI'SAL WIRDUL MAWROOD\nWoeful indeed will be the place to which they are led!\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قُتِلْتَ مَظْلُوْمًا\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QUTILTA MAZLOOMAA\nI bear witness that you were slain wrongly\nوَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُنْجِزٌ لَكُمْ مَا وَعَدَكُمْ\nWA ANNALLAAHA MUNJIZUN LAKUM MAA WA'ADAKUM\nand that Allah shall fulfill His promise to you.\nجِئْتُكَ زَاۤئِرًا عَارِفًا بِحَقِّكُمْ\nJI'TUKA ZAA'IRAN A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIKUM\nAs I am visiting you, I recognize your right,\nمُسَلِّمًا لَكُمْ\nMUSALLIMAN LAKUM\nI am submissive to you,\nتَابِعًا لِسُنَّتِكُمْ\nTAABI'AN LISUNNATIKUM\nI am imitating your course,\nوَنُصْرَتِيْ لَكُمْ مُعَدَّةٌ\nWA NUSRATEE LAKUM MU'ADDAH\nand I am preparing myself for supporting you\nحَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحَاكِمِيْنَ\nHATTAA YAHKUMALLAAHU WA HUWA KHAYRUL HAAKIMEEN\nuntil Allah judges, and He is the best of judges.\nفَمَعَكُمْ مَعَكُمْ\nFAMA'AKUM MA'AKUM\nSo, I am always with you\nلَا مَعَ عَدُوِّكُمْ\nLAA MA'A A'DUWWIKUM\nand I never am with your enemies.\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ\nSALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYKUM\nMay Allah’s blessings be upon you\nوَعَلٰى اَرْوَاحِكُمْ وَاَجْسَادِكُمْ\nWA A'LAA ARWAAHIKUM WA AJSAADIKUM\nand upon your souls and bodies\nوَشَاهِدِكُمْ وَغَاۤئِبِكُمْ\nWA SHAAHIDIKUM WA GHAA'IBIKUM\nand upon the present from you and the absent one.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nقَتَلَ اللّٰهُ اُمَّةً قَتَلَتْكُمْ بِالْاَيْدِيْ وَالْاَلْسُنِ\nQATALALLAAHU UMMATAN QATALATKUM BIL AYDEE WAL ALSUN\nMay Allah kill the people who killed you with their hands and their tongues.\nThen enter, go to the tomb and lean over it (or point towards it), and say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَبْدُ الصَّالِحُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'BDUS SAALIH\nPeace be upon you, O righteous servant (of Allah),\nالْمُطِيْعُ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلِاَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAL-MUTEE'U LILLAAHI WA LIRASOOLIHEE WA LI-AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nwho is obedient to Allah, to His Messenger, to the Commander of the Faithful,\nوَالْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nWAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nto al-Hasan, and to al-Husayn, peace be upon them.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَسَلَامٌ عَلٰى عِبَادِهِ الَّذِيْنَ اصْطَفٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI WA SALAAMUN A'LAA I'BAADIHIL LADHEENAS TAFAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nAll praise be to Allah, and peace be upon His servants whom He has chosen: Muhammad and his Household.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ وَمَغْفِرَتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUHOO WA MAGHFIRATUH\nPeace, Allah’s mercy, blessings and forgiveness be upon you\nوَعَلٰى رُوْحِكَ وَبَدَنِكَ\nWA A'LAA ROOHIKA WA BADANIK\nand upon your soul and your body.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ مَضَيْتَ عَلٰى مَا مَضٰى عَلَيْهِ الْبَدْرِيُّوْنَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA MADAYTA A'LAA MAA MADAA A'LAYHIL BADRIYYOON\nI bear witness that you died for the same principles for which the martyrs of the Battle of Badr died:\nالْمُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِي سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAL-MUJAAHIDOONA FEE SABEELILLAAH\nthose who strove in Allah’s way\nالْمُبَالِغُوْنَ فِيْ جِهَادِ اَعْدَاۤئِهٖ\nAL-MUBAALIGHOONA FEE JIHAADI A'DAA'IH\nand did their best in struggling against Allah’s enemies\nوَنُصْرَةِ اَوْلِيَاۤئِهٖ\nWA NUSRATI AWLIYAA'IH\nand in supporting Allah’s friends.\nفَجَزَاكَ اللّٰهُ اَفْضَلَ الْجَزَاۤءِ\nFAJAZAAKALLAAHU AFDALAL JAZAA'\nSo, may Allah reward you with the best rewarding,\nوَاَكْثَرَ الْجَزَاۤءِ\nWA AKTHARAL JAZAA'\nwith the most abundant rewarding,\nوَاَوْفَرَ جَزَاۤءِ اَحَدٍ مِمَّنْ وَفٰى بِبَيْعَتِهٖ\nWA AWFARA JAZAA'I AHADIN MIMMAN WAFAA BIBAY'ATIH\nand with the most affluent rewarding that He grants to one who fulfilled his allegiance to Him,\nوَاسْتَجَابَ لَهٗ دَعْوَتَهٗ\nWASTAJAABA LAHOO DA'WATAH\nresponded to His invitation,\nوَاَطَاعَ وُلَاةَ اَمْرِهٖ\nWA ATAA'A WULAATA AMRIH\nand obeyed His representatives.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ بَالَغْتَ فِي النَّصِيْحَةِ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD BAALAGHTA FIN NASEEHAH\nI bear witness that you exerted all efforts in acting sincerely\nوَاَعْطَيْتَ غَايَةَ الْمَجْهُوْدِ\nWA A'TAYTA GHAAYATAL MAJHOOD\nand you put forth all possible endeavors\nحَتّٰى بَعَثَكَ اللّٰهُ فِي الشُّهَدَاۤءِ\nHATTAA BA'ATHAKALLAAHU FISH SHUHADAA'\nso that Allah has included you with the martyrs,\nوَجَعَلَ رُوْحَكَ مَعَ اَرْوَاحِ السُّعَدَاۤءِ\nWA JA'ALA ROOHAKA MA'A ARWAAHIS SU'ADAA'\nput your soul with the souls of the delighted ones,\nوَاَعْطَاكَ مِنْ جِنَانِهٖ اَفْسَحَهَا مَنْزِلًا\nWA A'TAAKA MIN JINAANIHEE AFSAHAHAA MANZILAA\nhas decided for you the most spacious abode in the gardens of His Paradise\nوَاَفْضَلَهَا غُرَفًا\nWA AFDALAHAA GHURAFAA\nand the best rooms therein,\nوَرَفَعَ ذِكْرَكَ فِي الْعِلِّيِّيْنَ\nWA RAFA'A DHIKRAKA FIL I'LLIYYEEN\nraised your name in Illiyyin (the loftiest place),\nوَحَشَرَكَ مَعَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَالصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ\nWA HASHARAKA MA'AN NABIYYEENA WAS SIDDEEQEEN\nand added you to the group of the Prophets, the veracious ones,\nوَالشُّهَدَاۤءِ وَالصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWASH SHUHADAA'I WAS SAALIHEEN\nthe martyrs, and the righteous ones.\nوَحَسُنَ اُوْلٰۤئِكَ رَفِيْقًا\nWA HASUNA OOLAA'IKA RAFEEQAA\nand how excellent a company they are!\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ لَمْ تَهِنْ وَلَمْ تَنْكُلْ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA LAM TAHIN WA LAM TANKUL\nI bear witness that you never slackened or recoiled (from your duty)\nوَاَنَّكَ قَدْ مَضَيْتَ عَلٰى بَصِيْرَةٍ مِنْ اَمْرِكَ\nWA ANNAKA QAD MADAYTA A'LAA BASEERATIN MIN AMRIK\nand that you died while you are certain of your doctrine\nمُقْتَدِيًا بِالصَّالِحِيْنَ\nMUQTADIYAN BIS SAALIHEEN\nas you followed the righteous ones\nوَمُتَّبِعًا لِلنَّبِيِّيْنَ\nWA MUTTABI'AN LIN NABIYYEEN\nand imitated the Prophets.\nفَجَمَعَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ\nFAJAMA'ALLAAHU BAYNANAA WA BAYNAK\nSo, may Allah gather us with you\nوَبَيْنَ رَسُوْلِهٖ وَاَوْلِيَاۤئِهٖ\nWA BAYNA RASOOLIHEE WA AWLIYAA'IH\nand with His Messenger and intimate servants\nفِيْ مَنَازِلِ الْمُخْبِتِيْنَ\nFEE MANAAZILIL MUKHBITEEN\nin the abodes of the modest ones.\nفَاِنَّهٗ اَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nFA-INNAHOO ARHAMUR RAAHIMEEN\nSurely, He is the most merciful of all those who show mercy.\nThen pray two units at the head of the tomb and give them to him as a gift. After the prayer, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَلَا تَدَعْ لِيْ فِيْ هٰذَا الْمَكَانِ الْمُكَرَّمِ وَالْمَشْهَدِ الْمُعَظَّمِ ذَنْبًا اِلَّا غَفَرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA TADA' LEE FEE HAADHAL MAKAANIL MUKARRAMI WAL MASH-HADIL MU'AZZAMI DHANBAN ILLAA GHAFARTAH\nand do not leave me, in this honoured place and this glorified shrine, any sin but that You forgive it,\nوَلَا هَمًّا اِلَّا فَرَّجْتَهٗ\nWA LAA HAMMAN ILLAA FARRAJTAH\nany care but that You relieve it,\nوَلَا مَرَضًا اِلَّا شَفَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA MARADAN ILLAA SHAFAYTAH\nany illness but that You cure it,\nوَلَا عَيْبًا اِلَّا سَتَرْتَهٗ\nWA LAA A'YBAN ILLAA SATARTAH\nany defect but that You cover it,\nوَلَا رِزْقًا اِلَّا بَسَطْتَهٗ\nWA LAA RIZQAN ILLAA BASATTAH\nany sustenance but that You expand it,\nوَلَا خَوْفًا اِلَّا اٰمَنْتَهٗ\nWA LAA KHAWFAN ILLAA AAMANTAH\nany fear but that You turn it to safety,\nوَلَا شَمْلًا اِلَّا جَمَعْتَهٗ\nWA LAA SHAMLAN ILLAA JAMA'TAH\nany scattered affair but that You gather it,\nوَلَا غَاۤئِبًا اِلَّا حَفِظْتَهٗ وَاَدْنَيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA GHAA'IBAN ILLAA HAFIZTAHOO WA ADNAYTAH\nany absent one but that You guard him and bring him near,\nوَلَا حَاجَةً مِنْ حَوَاۤئِجِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWA LAA HAAJATAN MIN HAWAA'IJID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nand any of the needs of this world and the Hereafter\nلَكَ فِيْهَا رِضًى وَلِيَ فِيْهَا صَلَاحٌ\nLAKA FEEHAA RIDAN WA LIYA FEEHAA SALAAH\nin which there is Your pleasure and my good,\nاِلَّا قَضَيْتَهَا يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nILLAA QADAYTAHAA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nbut that You fulfil it, O most Merciful of the merciful.\nWhen you leave, bid him farewell with the farewell of al-Abbas (a.s.), at the end of [Ziyarat of Hazrat Abbas (a.s.) — Karbala](AG18).",
  "merits": "Muslim ibn Aqil was the son of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, and so a first cousin of Imam Husayn (a.s.). The Imam sent him as his envoy to Kufa, where the Umayyads killed him on the 9th of Dhul Hijjah. His shrine is by Masjid al-Kufah.\n\nMafatih al-Jinan gives this ziyarat after the acts of Masjid al-Kufah. In al-Mazar al-Kabir, the first part, said standing at the tomb, is the permission to enter; its author then says to enter, lean over the tomb (or point towards it, as in the earlier narration) and say the second part.\n\nThe dua after the prayer is the one said after the two-unit prayer at the shrine of al-Abbas (a.s.), in [Ziyarat of Hazrat Abbas (a.s.) — Karbala](AG18); here it is said after the prayer given to Muslim ibn Aqil."
